#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "Move them somewhere else, open the folder, and move them into it then."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "The private folder cannot be opened now: the screen is locked, or nothing here can watch for it to lock."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "Wrong password. Try again."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "The screen locked, so the private folder stays closed."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "Wrong password."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "The private folder could not be opened."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "There is a private folder already: ame security private-folder open"
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
#, sh-format
msgid "${PLAIN} is there already, and not an empty folder. Move what is in it somewhere else first."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "A folder in your home, Private, whose files are encrypted on their own, with a password of its own. It closes whenever the screen locks, before the computer sleeps and when you log out, and its key leaves memory then: someone who gets at the computer while it is locked, or takes it, cannot read it without the password. Open it again from Private Folder in the app grid."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "What it does not protect:"
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "  - copies made elsewhere: a program's own autosaves and backups, downloads, screenshots, the clipboard;"
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "  - a file open when the screen locks: the program that had it can no longer read it, and keeps what it had not saved in its window;"
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "  - while it is open, any program running as you can read it, as it can read the rest of your home."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "The encrypted copy, which backups and snapshots hold, shows the size of each file and the folders' shape, but no names and no contents."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "Choose its password next. Then a recovery key is shown, once: it is the only way back in without the password. Write it down and keep it somewhere safe, away from the computer."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "Make the private folder?"
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "The private folder was not made."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "Press Enter once you have written the recovery key down."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "Made. Open it now with the password you chose."
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "Change the private folder's password"
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "I know the password"
msgstr ""

#: usr/libexec/amethystora-private-folder
msgid "I have the recovery key"
msgstr ""

